    {
      "id": "plans_2026_06_15_redesign_01_repo_hardening_biome_migration",
      "label": "Biome Migration (ESLint replacement)",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-redesign-01-repo-hardening.md",
      "source_location": "Tasks 1-9",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Landed as one isolated commit before the redesign so the one-time reformat/class-sort never pollutes later diffs. useSortedClasses is a nursery rule with an Unsafe autofix, so the rule level is set to error and --write --unsafe is required for sorting to actually apply; opinionated recommended rules that flag intentional pre-existing patterns are deliberately downgraded to keep the swap behavior-preserving."
    },
    {
      "id": "plans_2026_06_15_redesign_01_repo_hardening_typed_env_module",
      "label": "Typed Env Module (zod, build-phase relaxed)",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-redesign-01-repo-hardening.md",
      "source_location": "Tasks 10-11",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "src/lib/env.ts is parsed once at import and transitively imported by the whole build graph, while the CI build sets only AUTH_SECRET + DATABASE_URL. Validation is therefore relaxed during NEXT_PHASE=phase-production-build (partial parse) and enforced fail-fast at runtime; empty strings map to undefined for optional vars because Vercel injects unset vars as ''."
    },
    {
      "id": "plans_2026_06_15_redesign_01_repo_hardening_playwright_scaffold",
      "label": "Playwright e2e Scaffold (Pixel 7, seeded e2e.db)",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-redesign-01-repo-hardening.md",
      "source_location": "Tasks 12-20",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "Mobile-first single Pixel 7 project; globalSetup rebuilds a clean seeded file:./data/e2e.db by redirecting DATABASE_URL, and auth uses the passcode path only because Google sign-in needs a real IdP. The CI e2e job is parallel and non-blocking (continue-on-error) while the suite is young \u2014 a signal, not a gate."
    },
    {
      "id": "plans_2026_06_15_redesign_01_repo_hardening_route_announcer_rule",
      "label": "Route-Announcer e2e Rule (never getByRole alert)",
      "file_type": "rationale",
      "source_file": "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-15-redesign-01-repo-hardening.md",
      "source_location": "Task 18",
      "source_url": null,
      "captured_at": null,
      "author": null,
      "contributor": null,
      "rationale": "The Next.js App Router renders a visually-hidden role=alert route announcer on every navigation, so asserting getByRole('alert') matches or races the announcer and produces flaky results; a persistent .claude/rules file prevents reintroduction."
    }
  ],
